Supervise git tunnels without client entry

Recover dead git tunnels as daemon-owned pod resources after
transport outages, tunnel process failures, and daemon restarts.
Serialize foreground and background setup so recovery cannot race a
concurrent enter.

Trigger pending branch pushes when the replacement tunnel refreshes
the pod's gateway configuration. The events stream now reports pod
state only and no longer performs a redundant, incorrectly ordered
recovery push.

Cover autonomous recovery for local Docker, SSH, and Kubernetes without
using rumpel enter as the repair trigger.
